WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.380
In 1921, Ludwig Wittgenstein
published a short, famous book.

2
00:00:05.430 --> 00:00:10.100
In it, a meaningful sentence is
a picture of a possible fact.

3
00:00:10.150 --> 00:00:13.860
God, ethics and the meaning
of life could not be pictured.

4
00:00:13.910 --> 00:00:16.110
They could only show themselves.

5
00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:19.780
Later, Wittgenstein rejected
his own picture theory.

6
00:00:19.830 --> 00:00:24.170
So does God mean the same in a prayer
as it would in a science report?

7
00:00:24.220 --> 00:00:27.770
In this mission, you'll meet his
later idea of language games,

8
00:00:27.820 --> 00:00:29.390
and forms of life.

9
00:00:29.440 --> 00:00:33.430
Then you'll weigh up the critics, who
ask whether believers mean their words as

10
00:00:33.480 --> 00:00:34.980
plain fact.

11
00:00:35.030 --> 00:00:39.810
Your mission: find out whether God
means the same in prayer as in science.
